  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "NflogTlv::getTotalSize",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/header/NflogLayer.h",
    "description": "Nflog TLV length parsing performs an out-of-bounds 2-byte read because validation only requires 2 bytes (`recordLen`) before constructing a TLV record, but subsequent logic (`getTotalSize()` and iteration in `TLVRecordReader`) dereferences fields beyond that (and may advance using attacker-controlled length). Specifically, `NflogTlv::canAssign()` accepts buffers with `tlvDataLen >= sizeof(recordLen)` instead of requiring the full TLV header (`recordLen` + `recordType`), so `getTotalSize()` reads `m_Data->recordLen` from pointers that can already be out of range during `getNextTLVRecord` traversal.",
    "conditions": "In FuzzTarget, attacker-controlled packet bytes are parsed into `Packet`, which invokes `NflogLayer::parseNextLayer()`, then `getTlvByType()` -> `TLVRecordReader::getTLVRecord()/getNextTLVRecord()`. A malformed/truncated NFLOG TLV area (including empty/short trailing bytes and crafted TLV lengths) causes the reader to treat an invalid next-record pointer as assignable due to weak `canAssign()` checks, then call `getTotalSize()` on it, triggering heap-buffer-overflow read."
  },
